---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { label } from "../i18n";
import {
  coverageMatrix,
  sourcingHealth,
  agencyLabel,
  nextUpdateDue,
  BACKFILL_START_FY,
  CONFIDENCE_MEANING,
  formatCr,
} from "../lib/data";

const { years, rows, totals } = coverageMatrix();
const health = sourcingHealth();
const pct = (n: number, d: number) => (d === 0 ? "0%" : `${Math.round((n / d) * 100)}%`);
const nextDue = nextUpdateDue().toLocaleDateString("en-IN", { month: "long", year: "numeric" });
---

<Base title="About the data">
  <h1>About the data</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A public, sourced record of what Karnataka's agencies have committed to build in Bengaluru. Here is what the
    figures mean, how sure we are of them, and how complete the record is.
  </p>

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
    <a href="#what-this-is">What this is</a>
    <a href="#confidence">Confidence</a>
    <a href="#data-quality">Data quality</a>
    <a href="#schedule">Update schedule</a>
    <a href="#open-data">Open data</a>
    <a href="#scope">Out of scope</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="what-this-is">
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      This site compiles publicly available information about infrastructure projects in Bengaluru from government
      budget documents, agency reports, audit reports and published news coverage. Every figure is shown with its
      source and the date it was recorded.
    </p>
    <p>
      Figures are drawn from official documents and media reports as published. They are not independently audited by
      us. Budget allocations, sanctioned amounts, funds released and actual expenditure are different things, and we
      label which is which. An allocation is not evidence that money was spent, and a delay is not evidence of
      wrongdoing.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not allege misconduct by any individual, official, department or contractor. Infrastructure delays have
      many causes, including land acquisition, litigation, clearances, funding, contractor capacity and design changes.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you believe something here is inaccurate, write to [email]. We check every report against our sources and
      publish a dated correction where warranted; see <a href="/updates?type=correction">corrections</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="confidence">
    <h2>How sure we are: confidence</h2>
    <p>Every project carries a confidence level, based on the strongest document behind its figures:</p>
    <dl class="fields confidence-list">
      {(["high", "medium", "low"] as const).map((c) => (
        <>
          <dt><span class={`confidence confidence-${c}`}>{label("confidence", c)}</span></dt>
          <dd>{CONFIDENCE_MEANING[c][0].toUpperCase() + CONFIDENCE_MEANING[c].slice(1)}.</dd>
        </>
      ))}
    </dl>
    <p>
      Right now {health.byConfidence.high} projects are high, {health.byConfidence.medium} medium and{" "}
      {health.byConfidence.low} low confidence. Lists only show the badge where a project differs from the rest; every
      project page states it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="data-quality">
    <h2>Data quality</h2>
    <p>
      Which years we have figures for, project by project. Hatched cells are gaps: years in which a project existed but
      no sourced figure has been found yet. We show the gaps on purpose.
    </p>

    <dl class="quality-strip">
      <div><dt>Project-years since FY{BACKFILL_START_FY} with a figure</dt><dd>{pct(totals.withFigure, totals.projectYears)}</dd><p>{totals.withFigure} of {totals.projectYears}</p></div>
      <div><dt>…backed by an official document</dt><dd>{pct(totals.withPrimary, totals.projectYears)}</dd><p>{totals.withPrimary} of {totals.projectYears}</p></div>
      <div><dt>Sources that are official documents</dt><dd>{totals.primarySources} / {totals.sources}</dd><p>the rest are news reports</p></div>
      <div><dt>Sources with an archived copy</dt><dd>{totals.archivedSources} / {totals.sources}</dd><p>government links break; archives don't</p></div>
    </dl>

    <div class="legend" aria-label="Legend">
      <span><i class="swatch cell-primary"></i>Official document</span>
      <span><i class="swatch cell-news"></i>News only</span>
      <span><i class="swatch cell-press_release"></i>Press release only</span>
      <span><i class="swatch cell-gap"></i>No figure found yet</span>
      <span><i class="swatch cell-na"></i>Before the project's first record</span>
      <span class="legend-kinds">A announced · S sanctioned · R revised cost · B bid · Rel released · U utilised</span>
    </div>

    <div class="card coverage-scroll">
      <table class="coverage">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" class="project-col">Project</th>
            {years.map((fy) => <th scope="col" class={fy < BACKFILL_START_FY ? "pre-window" : ""}>{fy}</th>)}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.map(({ project, cells }) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" class="project-col">
                <a href={`/projects/${project.id}`}>{project.name}</a>
                <span class="agency">{agencyLabel(project)}</span>
              </th>
              {cells.map((c) => {
                if (!c.applicable && c.entries.length === 0) return <td class="cell-na" title={`${c.fiscalYear}: before this project's first record`}></td>;
                if (c.entries.length === 0) return <td class="cell-gap" title={`${c.fiscalYear}: no figure found yet`}></td>;
                const kinds = [...new Set(c.entries.map((m) => label("kind_short", m.kind)))].join(" ");
                const detail = c.entries.map((m) => `${label("kind", m.kind)} ${formatCr(m.amount_cr)} (as of ${m.as_of})`).join("\n");
                return (
                  <td class={`cell-${c.strength}`} title={`${c.fiscalYear} · ${label("source_strength", c.strength!)}\n${detail}`}>{kinds}</td>
                );
              })}
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="footnote">
      Grouped by the fiscal year recorded on each figure; hover or long-press a cell for amounts. Want to fill a gap? See
      the <a href="https://github.com/littlemissbot/namma-blr/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md">contributor checklist</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="schedule">
    <h2>Update schedule</h2>
    <p>
      Every project is re-checked each quarter, in January, April, July and October, timed to when the underlying data
      moves: the Karnataka budget lands in spring, agency annual reports follow, and Assembly sessions produce question
      replies in batches. <strong>Next re-check: {nextDue}.</strong> Factual fixes are made any time between re-checks.
      A project not re-checked for two quarters is marked "possibly outdated". Each re-check's notes appear under{" "}
      <a href="/updates?type=sweep">Updates</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="open-data">
    <h2>Open data</h2>
    <p>
      The whole dataset is in a public Git repository, one file per record, so every change is auditable. Download the
      project list as <a href="/projects.csv">CSV</a> or <a href="/projects.json">JSON</a>, or follow updates by{" "}
      <a href="/changes.xml">RSS</a>. Source code:{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/littlemissbot/namma-blr">github.com/littlemissbot/namma-blr</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Until official files are obtained, Greater Bengaluru ward boundaries on the map are from OpenCity (CC BY 4.0)
      and older BBMP wards from the DataMeet India community (CC BY-SA 2.5 IN). Map tiles, project routes and lakes
      are © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="scope">
    <h2>Out of scope</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Allegations of corruption, or any claim about <em>why</em> a delay happened.</li>
      <li>Contractor performance rankings.</li>
      <li>Anything sourced only from social media or unattributed claims.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede { color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .toc { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem; margin: 1rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .toc a {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
  }
  .toc a:hover { border-color: var(--ink-muted); }
  section { scroll-margin-top: 1rem; }
  .confidence-list { max-width: 48rem; align-items: baseline; }

  .quality-strip {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(11rem, 1fr));
    margin: 1rem 0;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
  }
  .quality-strip > div { padding: 0.8rem 1rem 0.8rem 0; }
  .quality-strip > div + div { border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-left: 1rem; }
  .quality-strip dt { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .quality-strip dd { margin: 0.1rem 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.6rem; }
  .quality-strip p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .quality-strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .quality-strip > div:nth-child(odd) { border-left: none; padding-left: 0; }
  }

  .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 1.1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--ink-muted); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; }
  .swatch { display: inline-block; width: 0.9rem; height: 0.9rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); }
  .legend-kinds { flex-basis: 100%; }

  .coverage-scroll { overflow-x: auto; padding: 0; }
  .coverage { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.78rem; min-width: 100%; }
  .coverage th, .coverage td { border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 0.35rem 0.4rem; text-align: center; }
  .coverage thead th { font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .coverage thead th.pre-window { opacity: 0.6; }
  .project-col { position: sticky; left: 0; z-index: 1; background: var(--card-bg); text-align: left !important; min-width: 11rem; max-width: 16rem; }
  .project-col a { font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .project-col a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .agency { display: block; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .coverage td { font-weight: 600; min-width: 2.6rem; }
  .cell-primary { background: var(--status-complete-bg); color: var(--status-complete); }
  .cell-news { background: var(--status-progress-bg); color: var(--status-progress); }
  .cell-press_release { background: var(--status-stalled-bg); color: var(--status-stalled); }
  .cell-gap { background: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, transparent 0 4px, var(--rule) 4px 5px); }
  .cell-na { background: var(--paper-raised); }
  .footnote { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ink-muted); margin-top: 0.75rem; }
</style>
